# Runtime state written by utils/file (per-world building records, etc.)
state/

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# Dev-only trees: scratch references and the legacy PalSmith code kept on disk for
# reference while porting.
#
# Scripts/palforge/test/ IS NOT HERE, and it was once a real defect rather than a judgement
# call. There used to be two trees one character apart — test/ and tests/ — and tests/ was
# listed on this line while being LIVE CODE that core/registry.lua required at startup. A clone
# therefore had a boot path and a console command pointing at files the repository did not
# carry. There is ONE tree now, it ships, and `tools/deploy.sh --release` is what keeps it out
# of a player's copy — a build step rather than an ignore rule, which is the right altitude for
# "this is not part of a release".
#
# /tests/ below is ROOT-anchored and is a different tree entirely — the Python/Mojo scratch
# harness at the repo root — so it stays ignored and does not reach anything under Scripts/.
tmp/
/tests/
deprecated/

