# plan
plan/

# dumps
# Measured reflection data recovered from a real session. reflection/, catalog/ and cxx/ are
# the evidence plan/TODO.md cites — they are the difference between "we measured this" and
# "someone has to boot the game and measure it again", so they ship. The rest is scratch.
#
# cxx/ is DELIBERATELY NOT SHIPPED. It is UE4SS's own CXXHeaderDump of the installed binary —
# 1579 headers carrying every UFunction's real signature, and the single most useful artifact
# in this project's history: give, take, spawning, DataTable reads, status effects and skill
# lists were all diagnosed from it. But it is reverse-engineered class declarations from a
# commercial game's shipping executable, which is a different thing from the row data in
# catalog/ and the name lists in reflection/, and it does not belong in a public repository.
#
# Regenerate it locally in one action — UE4SS GUI console, "Dump CXX Headers" — and it lands in
# Pal/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/CXXHeaderDump/. dumps/cxx/README.md (also untracked) explains how to
# read it. Every fact this tree took FROM it is quoted inline at the call site with a file:line
# citation, so no finding depends on having the dump to hand.
dumps/*
!dumps/reflection/
!dumps/catalog/
# Written into the DEPLOYED copy by tools/deploy.sh so a stale in-game run is visible in
# the log. Never part of the source tree.
Scripts/palforge/build.lua

# THE DEV OVERLAY, and the reason it is listed here is a release gate rather than tidiness.
# main.lua requires `palforge_dev` immediately before registry.initialize() and ignores it when
# absent; the file sets env.dev = true and env.debug = true, which arms the nine dev keybinds —
# one of them, F4, unlocks EVERY technology in the loaded save — plus the F1 API suite, F9
# reload and the test bundles. `dev = true` was once the shipped default in env.lua and that is
# exactly what this line exists to prevent happening a second time: the switch now lives in a
# file that tools/deploy.sh writes into a DEPLOYED tree (default mode), deletes with --release,
# and that can never travel to a player through the repository.
Scripts/palforge_dev.lua

# Build output. `tools/deploy.sh --package` (npm run package) stages the release tree and the
# zip here; the release workflow builds it fresh on every run and uploads it, so a copy checked
# in would only ever be an out-of-date one claiming to be the download.
/dist/

# Rendered artwork. `npm run art` regenerates every PNG from the SVGs in assets/, which are the
# source. Committing them would let a stale PNG sit on a mod page after the design changed —
# and the design HAS changed once already, when the anvil turned out to rasterise into something
# closer to a bowtie than a tool.
publish/images/
